Engine: CMEV's missile merge and removal only for a live missile (open fix 63).

STATUS: APPLIED 1 October 2026 by work order 197 (Part B.2, "exercise every
CMEV event kind ... correct what is off") — orion2re ee844b0b on
orionlayer-local (before: 6f69de27), this file's diff byte for byte (index
lines included). Required by tools/version_check.py since work order 197.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_combat_events_merge.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert ee844b0b` or
`patch -R -p1`, and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    The first battle with missiles (work order 197's scratch game: three
    Doom Stars at Draconis) sent 287 "missile merge" and 294 "missile gone"
    events for 15 launches. The original's merge loop in Fire_Missile_
    (cmbtmis.cpp) goes on after Kill_Missile_ has zeroed the merged
    missile, and every EMPTY slot then matches the zeroed record (type 0,
    target 0, x 0, y 0): the game adds 0 to it and kills the empty missile
    again — harmless, and left exactly as it is. Open fix 56's two hooks
    reported each of those calls. Now each hook reports only while the
    missile it names is live (type above WEAPON_NO_WEAPONS): the one real
    merge, and each real removal. Checked against the state blocks by
    tools/combat_consistency.py: 572 of 645 events off before, 0 of 73 after.

    Written inside the existing #ifdef ORION2RE_EXT blocks of open fix 56 in
    src/game/cmbtmis.cpp, one line before each hook; fix 56's own lines are
    unchanged. Nothing runs without the extension, and with it only what is
    reported changes: an engine without OrionLayer behaves exactly as
    before. One marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 63.`, on one line at each of
    the two changed places.

diff --git a/src/game/cmbtmis.cpp b/src/game/cmbtmis.cpp
index 60b2679a..321ed49f 100644
--- a/src/game/cmbtmis.cpp
+++ b/src/game/cmbtmis.cpp
@@ -1039,6 +1039,7 @@ namespace CMBTMIS {
 
     void __cdecl Kill_Missile_(int16_t missile_idx) {
 #ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+        if (MOX::_missile[missile_idx].type > WEAPON_NO_WEAPONS)  // OrionLayer, open fix 63. An empty slot killed again is no missile gone.
         ext::Combat_Event(ext::CEV_MISSILE_GONE, missile_idx, MOX::_missile[missile_idx].type, MOX::_missile[missile_idx].quantity, MOX::_missile[missile_idx].x, MOX::_missile[missile_idx].y);  // OrionLayer, open fix 56.
 #endif
         // Clear the missile data structure
@@ -1289,6 +1290,7 @@ namespace CMBTMIS {
 
                         MOX::_missile[i].quantity += MOX::_missile[missile_idx].quantity;
 #ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+                        if (MOX::_missile[missile_idx].type > WEAPON_NO_WEAPONS)  // OrionLayer, open fix 63. Once killed, the loop matches every empty slot: no event for those.
                         ext::Combat_Event(ext::CEV_MISSILE_MERGE, missile_idx, i, MOX::_missile[i].quantity);  // OrionLayer, open fix 56.
 #endif
                         Kill_Missile_(missile_idx);
